Subject: base-files: wait for procd's sysupgrade result without a deadline

The ubus client's default 30-second timeout does not cancel procd's
sysupgrade handler. If validation takes longer, sysupgrade exits while
procd is still using the image. The daemon then releases its update gate
and a retry can overwrite that image before procd flashes it.

Wait without a client deadline. Procd returns an error on rejection; a
successful handoff stops the daemon before flashing the image in place.

Start9 downstream patch (start-technologies projects/start-wrt).
Applies to: openwrt v25.12.6

--- a/package/base-files/files/sbin/sysupgrade
+++ b/package/base-files/files/sbin/sysupgrade
@@ -448,5 +448,6 @@
 	[ $USE_CURR_PART -eq 1 ] && json_add_boolean use_curr_part 1
 	json_close_object
 
-	ubus call system sysupgrade "$(json_dump)"
+	# A client timeout does not cancel procd's pending flash.
+	ubus -t 0 call system sysupgrade "$(json_dump)"
 fi
